  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations for janitorial services (NAICS 561720) total $1.1B in FY2026 to date. Award activity shows 4,086 awards with an average award size of $281K. Obligations are down 35.7% year over year, following a multi-year period when annual obligations ranged from $1.6B to $1.8B: FY21 $1.6B, FY22 $1.6B, FY23 $1.7B, FY24 $1.7B, and FY25 $1.8B. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, with $705M in obligations through the current fiscal year. Other buyers with meaningful obligations include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $86.8M, the Department of Homeland Security at $67.9M, and the General Services Administration at $60.5M. The vendor market is led by a small group of contractors: GLOBAL CONNECTIONS TO EMPLOYMENT, INC. at $44M and TEYA SUPPORT SERVICES LLC at $39.8M, followed by several firms in the $21.2M to $39.2M range. These figures are partial, fiscal year to date totals, so annual totals may change as the fiscal year progresses.",
    "sections": [
