        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, with $705M in obligations for FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows at $86.8M, then the Department of Homeland Security at $67.9M and the General Services Administration at $60.5M. Several civilian agencies also show consistent spend, including HHS at $43.2M and DOT at $43M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does vendor concentration look like in this market?",
        "body": "The top vendors account for multi‑million dollar obligations, led by GLOBAL CONNECTIONS TO EMPLOYMENT, INC. at $44M and TEYA SUPPORT SERVICES LLC at $39.8M. Other leading contractors include FEDCAP REHABILITATION SERVICES, INC at $39.2M and PROFESSIONAL CONTRACT SERVICES, INC. at $37.7M. The ten largest vendors listed have obligations ranging from $21.2M to $44M."
      }
